{{~##
   One declared record type, and the levels inside it that are its own.

   **A struct is an entity beside a table and an enum, so it gets a header like one.** The
   declaration says "this is one type", and the generated code says the same thing only if
   there is one type - and these are file-scope structs, so a type declared per table would be
   the same name declared twice. spec/types/declared-struct-identity.md.
##~}}
{{ include 'cpp-file-head.sbn' ~}}
{{~ for rt in record.types }}
{{~ if rt.is_outermost ~}}
{{~ if record.comment | array.size > 0 ~}}
{{~ for line in record.comment ~}}
/// {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ else ~}}
/// One value of the declaration that names it.
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ else ~}}
/// A record inside {{ record.name }}.
{{~ end ~}}
{{ include 'cpp-record-body.sbn' ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{ include 'cpp-file-foot.sbn' ~}}
